.TH WERKMEISTER-WORKSPACE 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-workspace \- Create a new workspace under $WERKMEISTER_WORKSPACES_ROOT (git worktrees on a \e<user>/\e<workspace> branch) and run init\-workspace inside it.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister workspace\fR [feature]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-issue\-id <ref>\fR
Issue ID in this machine's issue tracker (see \fBwerkmeister setup\fR). Its slug is prefixed to the workspace dir name; passed through to init\-workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-project <name>\fR
The project (projects: in ~/.werkmeister/config.yaml) whose tracker holds the issue. Default: the one whose scope holds \-\-issue\-id, else the default project.
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-services <list>\fR
Comma\-separated services to run locally. Their owning repos are added as worktrees, and the list is passed through to init\-workspace.
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-repos <list>\fR
Comma\-separated repos to create worktrees for (union with the repos derived from \-\-services). Interactive multi\-select if neither \-\-repos nor \-\-services is given.
.TP
\fB\-\-labels <list>\fR
Comma\-separated free\-form tags for filtering workspaces in the dashboard search; passed through to init\-workspace.
.TP
\fB\-t, \-\-task <title>\fR
Task title for the workspace CLAUDE.md; passed through to init\-workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-test\-path <path>\fR
URL path for feature testing; passed through to init\-workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-description <text>\fR
Free\-form description for the CLAUDE.md header; passed through to init\-workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-starting\-prompt <text>\fR
First instruction for the agent; passed through to init\-workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-work\-type <type>\fR
Kind of work; seeds the first\-phase handoff note. Passed through to init\-workspace.
.TP
\fB\-\-context\-strategy <id>\fR
Context layer to generate: jit (skills, hooks, notes) or icm (staged folders). (env: WERKMEISTER_CONTEXT_STRATEGY; config: context_strategy).
.TP
\fB\-\-autonomous\fR
Run an icm workspace stage\-to\-PR with no human checks, and allow the Bash calls a headless session needs (env: WERKMEISTER_AUTONOMOUS; config: autonomous).
.TP
\fB\-\-model <id>\fR
Claude model for this workspace's sessions: an alias (opus, sonnet, haiku) or a claude\-… id; blank keeps Claude Code's default (env: WERKMEISTER_MODEL; config: model).
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-stop\fR
Stop this workspace's feature containers when a Claude session in it ends and no other is open (a SessionEnd hook; env: WERKMEISTER_AUTO_STOP; config: auto_stop).
.TP
\fB\-\-browser\-form\fR
Collect inputs through the Werkmeister\-branded browser form (the same form the Desktop MCP App renders), pre\-filled from every flag given, then create the workspace. Opens a localhost page in the default browser and blocks until submit/cancel.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-distill\fR
Store the issue but don't have a model rewrite it into description/starting_prompt.
.TP
\fB\-\-open\fR
With \-\-browser\-form: launch VS Code on the new workspace after creating.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Delete a \e<user>/\e<workspace> branch an earlier workspace of the same name left on origin, instead of aborting (that branch's work is gone; see the abort message for how to continue it instead).
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Creates a new workspace under the workspaces root and initializes it. It resolves its inputs (flags, an existing \fBworkspace.yml\fR, or the interactive wizard), creates the workspace folder as a git worktree of the workspace record repo (\fBoverrides.workspace_repo\fR) on a \fBuser/workspace\fR branch, writes \fB.werkmeister/workspace.yml\fR, and runs \fBwerkmeister init\-workspace\fR inside it. The initial state is committed, not pushed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister workspace my\-feature \-\-issue\-id SW\-180 \-\-services backend,frontend
werkmeister workspace my\-feature \-\-context\-strategy icm \-\-work\-type refactor
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBwerkmeister init\-workspace\fR owns everything derived from \fBworkspace.yml\fR; \fBwerkmeister close\-out\fR ends a workspace.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
